<div><font face=3D"Calibri">&nbsp;</font></div>
<div><font face=3D"Calibri">In my previous e-mail I requested you to enumer=
ate changes that are made to the driver, compared to the previous version(s=
). There were also a few questions that I did not get answer for.</font></d=
iv>
<div><font face=3D"Calibri" color=3D"blue">In order to improve flash read/w=
rite security of boot loader. We increase handshake flow and command sequen=
ce complexity. Our previous flash write functions are single side action. N=
ew version we increase more handshake
flow to check data accuracy. Firmware update flow increases as below:</font=
></div>
<ol style=3D"margin:0;padding-left:18pt;">
<font face=3D"Calibri" color=3D"blue">
<li>Check firmware file size, if file size is null, return fail.<font color=
=3D"#1F497D"> </font></li><li>Check touch MCU run on main firmware or boot =
loader. Both cases have different return values. In case of flash write fun=
ction, if touch MCU work on main code<font face=3D"Courier New" color=3D"#1=
F497D">,</font> <font color=3D"#1F497D">t</font>ouch driver need
issue enter boot loader command to touch MCU and wait for MCU boot mode rea=
dy.</li><li>Turn off touch MCU<font color=3D"#1F497D"> </font>watchdog func=
tion to prevent interference.</li><li>Check boot loader write state path re=
ady<font face=3D"Courier New" color=3D"#1F497D">.</font></li><li>Send boot =
mode trigger command to unlock flash<font face=3D"Courier New" color=3D"#1F=
497D">-</font>write-protection<font face=3D"Courier New" color=3D"#1F497D">=
.</font></li><li>Execute page write command. Each write command will wait t=
ouch MCU acknowledge and then execute next step.</li><li>Leave boot loader =
to check firmware work.</li><li>Raydium touch driver check touch MCU work o=
n main firmware or not. If touch MCU work on main firmware and return corre=
ct acknowledge to kernel, this means flash write command success.</li><li>W=
